{"hits": {"hits": [{"metadata": {"authors": [{"full_name": "Butenschoen, Mathias"}, {"full_name": "Kniehl, Bernd A."}], "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "84", "artid": "051501", "year": 2011, "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.D"}], "texkeys": ["Butenschoen:2011yh"], "abstracts": [{"value": "We calculate the cross sections of inclusive J/psi production in photoproduction and two-photon scattering, involving both direct and resolved photons, and in e^+e^- annihilation at next-to-leading order (NLO) within the factorization formalism of nonrelativistic quantum chromodynamics (NRQCD), including the full relativistic corrections due to the intermediate ^1S_0^{[8]}, ^3S_1^{[8]}, and ^3P_J^{[8]} color-octet (CO) states. Exploiting also our previous results on hadroproduction, we perform a combined fit of the respective CO long-distance matrix elements (LDMEs) to all available high-quality data of inclusive J/psi production, from KEKB, LEP~II, RHIC, HERA, the Tevatron, and the LHC, comprising a total of 194 data points from 26 data sets."}], "control_number": 898069, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevD.84.051501"}], "arxiv_eprints": [{"value": "1105.0820"}], "titles": [{"title": "World data of J/psi production consolidate NRQCD factorization at NLO"}, {"title": "World data of J/psi production consolidate NRQCD factorization at NLO"}], "author_count": 2, "document_type": ["article"]}, "updated": "2023-03-07T02:17:35.779534+00:00", "created": "2011-05-04T00:00:00+00:00", "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/898069?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/898069?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/898069?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/898069?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/898069?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/898069?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refers